# The build context.
#
# The Dockerfile in docker/ deliberately COPYs nothing -- you bind-mount the
# working tree into the running container instead -- but Docker still tars up
# and sends the entire context to the daemon before it starts. Without this
# file every `docker build` would ship .toolchain/ (160 MB of unpacked .deb
# files) and the whole .git object store, on every single build.
#
# Note for the curious: a .dockerignore here does not affect `docker run -v`,
# which mounts your real tree. It only shrinks what gets sent to the builder.

.git
.toolchain

build/
firmware/build/

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Nothing here is an input to the image. If a Dockerfile ever grows a COPY,
# add the pattern back at that point rather than loosening this file.
docker/
docs/
*.md